{"name":"Valentino Nero","hex":"#382c38","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Valentino nero","blocks":[{"text":"Valentino nero is a red Italian wine grape variety that is grown in the Piedmont wine region of northwest Italy but was initially bred at the Conegliano research center in the Veneto. In 1936, its creator, Giovanni Dalmasso, stated that the grape was a crossing of two Vitis vinifera Piedmontese varieties, Nebbiolo and Dolcetto, but DNA profiling in 2009 showed that the French wine grape Chatus and Dolcetto were the parent vines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Dolcetto_grapes.JPG/330px-Dolcetto_grapes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentino_nero","wikidata":"Q17119338"},{"title":"Nero","blocks":[{"text":"Nero Claudius Caesar Augustus Germanicus was Roman emperor from AD 54 until his suicide in AD 68. He was the final emperor of the Julio-Claudian dynasty, which comprised the first five emperors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Nero_Glyptothek_Munich_321.jpg/330px-Nero_Glyptothek_Munich_321.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nero","wikidata":"Q1413"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Ard%C3%A8che-Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Ard%C3%A8che-Position.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The Ardèche region in France where Valentino nero's other parent variety, Chatus, originated","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArd%C3%A8che-Position.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Great_Cameo_of_France-removebg.png/330px-Great_Cameo_of_France-removeb